@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<h1 class="mb-1">Privacy</h1>
<p class="text-muted mb-4">How HomeVault handles your data.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">What we store</h4>
<p class="small">
    Only what you provide: a username, a password, your name and address,
    and the items you choose to catalog. Nothing else is collected.
</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">How passwords are handled</h4>
<p class="small">
    Passwords are hashed with BCrypt before they are written to the
    database. Plaintext passwords are never persisted and cannot be
    recovered — only verified at login time.
</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">Data isolation</h4>
<p class="small">
    Every catalog operation is scoped to the CatalogId stored in your
    auth cookie. The database queries themselves filter by that id, so a
    user cannot see or modify another user's items even with a crafted
    request.
</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">Third parties</h4>
<p class="small">
    HomeVault uses no third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking.
    No data leaves the application's own database.
</p>